All 16 dataset definitions, including ChemVQA-2K-spacing-v1, and the generic
rubric are retained with their scoring, image inspection, parsing, and prompt
helpers. Strict-category rubrics, custom strict-ceiling prompts/scoring, repair
prompts, and upstream orchestration are excluded. Generic scoring retains its
own prompts and equal-weight mean without dataset caps.
Formatting/import cleanup is applied; retained scoring semantics are unchanged.
Gym requires explicit rubric names; unused filename-based rubric inference,
the duplicate prompt wrapper, and the no-op whitespace compatibility option
have been removed. Runtime orchestration uses Gym APIs rather than the upstream package.
Judge image MIME types are detected from content to match Gym preparation,
including references without a filename extension. Scoring and prompt text are unchanged.
Golden fixtures were generated from this source checkout, not from the port.

The source checkout was modified. Exact source SHA-256 hashes are recorded in
tests/fixtures/provenance.json, including the existing EEE background revision
and whitespace-diagnostic behavior, plus the generic source hash. The base commit
alone does not identify it.

Image similarity and Blend A aggregation use the source protocol pinned by
image_metrics_source_sha256 in the provenance file. Golden image-metric fixtures
record the modified source outputs; no external repository is needed at runtime.

